#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# with_cleanup

#% text
# `with_cleanup(body, cleanup)` evaluates `body`, then `cleanup`, and gives the value of `body`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `with_cleanup(init, body, cleanup)` evaluates `init` first.

#% item
# The cleanup runs also when the body gives a failure or throws a value: the failure is the result, and an outer `catch` takes a thrown value.

#% item
# An interrupt or an exhausted limit stops the whole evaluation, the cleanup with it.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
with_cleanup({ x = 7; x^2 }, unset(x))
#% output
#= 49

#% cell
x
#% output
#= x

#% cell
catch(with_cleanup(print(1), { throw(done); print(2) }, print(3)))
#% output
#| 1
#| 3
#= done

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `catch`, `throw`, `check`
